{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>And bless himself in his heart.</b> A term of blessing — he reckons in his heart a blessing of peace for himself, saying: these curses will not come upon me; rather, <b>peace will be mine.</b>" "<b>And bless himself.</b> בנדי״רא שו״יא בְּלַעַז — like וְהִתְגַּלָּח, and וְהִתְפַּלֵּל." "<b>When I walk in the stubbornness of my heart.</b> In what my heart sees — as in (Numbers 24) ״אֲשׁוּרֶנּוּ וְלֹא קָרוֹב״ — that is, what my heart sees to do." "<b>To sweep away the moist.</b> Because he adds punishment upon him for what he did until now unwittingly — and I would have passed over them — and now he causes that I combine the unwitting with the intentional and exact everything from him. And thus Onkelos renders: ״בְּדִיל לְאוֹסָפָא לֵהּ חֶטְיֵי שָׁלוּתָא עַל זְדָנוּתָא״ — that I add to him the unwitting upon the intentional." "<b>The moist.</b> Unwitting — for he acts like a drunkard, who acts without knowledge." "<b>Parched thirst.</b> That he does it knowingly and with desire."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 29, :notes {1 "The la'az is Old French se vanter or bénir; the exact word behind בנדי״רא שו״יא is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:48:55.237530519Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}